.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
something that can be automatically moved, spun or resized over time\&. 


.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
\fBAPI Stability: 2 — Evolving\fP\&. This API is implemented and supported, but its contract is still settling\&. Compatibility is preserved where practical; breaking changes are documented in release notes\&. See \fBAPI stability\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBAnimated\fP separates immediate edits and constant rates from scheduled transitions\&. All animation durations and waits use floating-point seconds\&. Setters are immediate and chainable; they cannot consume a \fBwait()\fP or \fBandThen()\fP\&. Timed change methods require explicit seconds; explicit zero applies immediately outside a sequence\&. To names specify targets; By names specify additive deltas\&. \fBgrow()\fP and \fBstretch()\fP use factors and change logical size; \fBchangeScaleTo()\fP/changeScaleBy() change the independent transform scale\&. Constant rates continue after a rate transition ends\&.

.PP
Scheduled operations normally run concurrently\&. \fBandThen()\fP sequences the next operation after the most recently scheduled one; \fBwait()\fP delays the next timed request\&. Immediate calls after either throw before changing state\&. \fBcancelSchedule()\fP clears pending sequencing and scheduled work while retaining current constant rates\&.

.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
sprite\&.setMovement(40, 0);
sprite\&.changeMovementTo(0, 0, 0\&.5); // Ease the rate to a stop in half a second\&.
sprite\&.setGrowing(8);             // Add eight logical size units per second\&.
sprite\&.changeGrowingTo(0, 0\&.25);  // Ease the growth rate to zero\&.

.fi
.PP
.RE
.PP
\fBPhysicsBody\fP owns physical velocity, mass, damping, forces and impulses\&.

.PP
It has no drawing capabilities, so it is not intended to be used directly in most cases, but rather as a base class for items that can be animated\&. It could be used on a server to drive animation that is rendered on the client\&.

.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBSprite\fP 

.PP
\fBSpriteLayer\fP 
.RE
.PP

