.PP 
.SS "\fBAnimated\fP addAnimationHelper (\fBIAnimationHelper\fP helper)"

.PP
Register a callback after the object's normal animation step\&. The callback runs as \fRcallback\&.call(helper, owner, deltaSeconds)\fP and returns a boolean: true keeps its registration, false retires it\&. Helpers run in registration order\&. Adding the same helper twice to one owner has no effect; a helper may also be registered on several owners\&. A retained helper can be added again after it finishes\&.

.PP
Callbacks may remove themselves, remove another helper, or clear the owner's helpers\&. Removed callbacks do not run later in the same step\&. Additions first run on the next step\&. Removing and re-adding the current helper creates a new registration, which is unaffected by the old callback returning false\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIhelper\fP An \fBIAnimationHelper\fP constructed from a callback\&. Active registrations retain it\&. After retirement, normal JavaScript references determine its lifetime\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The original owner object, for chaining\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
const helper = new pdg\&.IAnimationHelper(function(owner, deltaSeconds) {
    owner\&.rotateBy(deltaSeconds * 0\&.5);
    return true;
});
sprite\&.addAnimationHelper(helper)\&.setMovement(20, 0);
// Later: sprite\&.removeAnimationHelper(helper);

.fi
.PP
 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBremoveAnimationHelper()\fP, \fBclearAnimationHelpers()\fP, \fBIAnimationHelper\fP 
.RE
.PP

.PP
References \fBAnimated()\fP\&.
.SS "\fBAnimated\fP andAlso ()"

.PP
Join the following operand to the preceding parallel chain\&. 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This object for chaining\&. Requires a preceding operand that has not activated and a following operand\&. Repeated calls extend an implied batch\&. Following \fBuntil()\fP, \fByoyo()\fP, \fBrepeat()\fP, timing, amplitude and playback controls select that complete chain\&. Inside a series, the chain is one step and the next ordinary operand waits for every member to complete\&. Pending explicit \fBandThen()\fP placement is incompatible with \fBandAlso()\fP\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
target\&.series()\&.moveBy(100, 0, 2)\&.andAlso()\&.rotateBy(1, 2)
    \&.endSeries();

.fi
.PP
 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBbatch()\fP, \fBuntil()\fP, \fBseries()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.PP
References \fBAnimated()\fP\&.
.SS "\fBAnimated\fP andThen ()"

.PP
Start the next timed operation after the most recently scheduled operation finishes\&. Uses the selected operation or block, rather than all concurrent work\&. Script dependencies observe actual completion, including repeat, timing modifiers, and \fBuntil()\fP\&. The next request consumes this sequencing state; later calls again run concurrently unless sequenced\&. A successor acquires its properties and resolves relative targets when it starts\&. Inside script construction, immediate commands are recorded and run at activation; ordinary immediate calls outside construction retain their existing restrictions\&. \fBandThen()\fP\&.wait(seconds) composes completion with a delay\&. No then() method is provided, so returning an \fBAnimated\fP object from an async JavaScript function is safe\&.

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This object, for chaining\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBwait()\fP, \fBcancelSchedule()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.PP
References \fBAnimated()\fP\&.
.SS "boolean animate (number deltaSeconds)"

.PP
Advance programmed animation by elapsed seconds\&. Advances constant rates, scheduled animations and helpers\&. MVC controllers advance their Views automatically\&. Standalone \fBAnimatedAttributes\fP instances must be advanced explicitly; \fBDrawing\fP copies \fBAttributes\fP samples\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIdeltaSeconds\fP Finite nonnegative elapsed seconds\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
True if any animation value changed\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBpauseSchedule()\fP, \fBaddAnimationHelper()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBAnimated\fP batch ()"

.PP
Open an anonymous animation block\&. 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This object for chaining\&. Children run concurrently by default\&. \fBandThen()\fP establishes a completion dependency; \fBwait()\fP delays the following child without joining earlier children\&. Construction remains local until \fBendBatch()\fP; the new context has no preceding operand\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBNative animation scripts\fP 
.RE
.PP

.PP
References \fBAnimated()\fP\&.
.SS "\fBAnimated\fP cancelSchedule ()"

.PP
Discard scheduled animations and pending sequencing\&. Keeps current values, constant rates and the paused state\&. Clears pending \fBwait()\fP/andThen() state\&. \fBAnimatedAttributes\fP also clears appearance and frame transitions\&.

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This object, for chaining\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBhasScheduledAnimations()\fP, \fBpauseSchedule()\fP 
.RE
.PP

