.SS "\fBAnimated\fP changeGrowingBy (number amountPerSecond, number durationSeconds, int easing = \fR\fBlinearTween\fP\fP)"

.PP
Animate the growing rate by an additive delta\&. 
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Parameter \fReasing:\fP \fBEasingFunction\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
Uses logical units per second equally on both axes\&. Duration is the time to reach the new rate, not the lifetime of the motion: the final rate continues until changed or stopped\&. With \fBandThen()\fP, the delta is added to the rate when this operation starts\&. Logical size changes independently of transform scale\&. Durations are explicit floating-point seconds\&. Zero applies immediately; a request after \fBwait()\fP or \fBandThen()\fP must have positive duration\&.

