.SS "boolean deleteScript (string name)\fR [static]\fP"

.PP
Remove a definition and release its memory in the shared script library\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIname\fP Nonempty script name\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
True if the definition existed and was removed; false otherwise\&. This is a static method, also available on animated class constructors such as \fBSprite\fP, \fBCamera\fP, \fBPart\fP and \fBTroupe\fP\&. All class entry points use the same library\&. Running instances continue using their published copies\&. Deleted names can be redefined\&. Any retained recorder rejects further use; its definition graph is released at deletion, while its small wrapper survives until garbage collection\&. An empty name throws\&.
.RE
.PP
.PP
.nf
pdg\&.Animated\&.defineScript('leave')\&.moveBy(100, 0, 0\&.5)\&.endScript();
sprite\&.playScript('leave');
pdg\&.Animated\&.deleteScript('leave'); // the running instance still finishes
.fi
