.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIname\fP Nonempty mark name, unique within its script invocation\&. 
.br
\fIsaveState\fP Whether arrival saves the target's animated channel values, ordinary animation tracks and script execution cursor; default true\&. Each later arrival replaces that invocation's saved state\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This object for chaining\&. Recording the mark does not capture state\&. In a series, the mark is reached after the preceding step completes; in a batch, placement remains parallel unless \fBandThen()\fP provides a dependency\&. \fBTroupe\fP marks save each member's state\&. Marks belong to independent playback instances, not the shared definition\&. State does not include physics, artwork ownership, application data or \fBTroupe\fP membership\&. Blocks containing marks or jumps reject \fByoyo()\fP, amplitude and clock modifiers\&. Full snapshots preserve mark names, saved values, ordinary animation tracks and the playback cursor needed by \fBjumpToMark()\fP\&. Unvisited marks retain no saved state; jumps to them continue after the mark without restoring state\&. Individual supported animations within such a block can still be modified\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBjumpToMark()\fP, \fBseries()\fP 
.RE
