.SS "\fBAnimated\fP triggerEvent (string name)"

.PP
Emit a custom named animation event or record an event step\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIname\fP Custom nonempty name\&. Built-in animation event names and the eventType_ namespace are reserved\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This animated object for chaining\&.
.RE
.PP
During script recording, inside \fBbatch()\fP/series(), or after \fBandThen()\fP, this records a zero-time step\&. Playback emits the event whenever execution reaches that step, including repeat visits\&. Otherwise it emits immediately on the selected animation\&. Subscribe with on(name, handler); custom events propagate to enclosing blocks\&. This does not post numeric PDG events\&. Invalid or reserved names raise an error before modifying the script\&. Portable snapshots preserve custom event names and playback cursors\&. Receivers may register handlers after restoration; events without handlers are harmless\&. Registered callback functions remain unsupported in portable snapshots\&. 
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBon()\fP, \fBseries()\fP, \fBandThen()\fP 
.RE
.PP

